The fresh false-postcondition probe behaved correctly: it parsed and dry-ran successfully, then failed with `WarnStuckClaimState` on the expected impossible equality `lengthString(S) + 1 = lengthString(S)`. The theorem is result-constraining and body-sensitive; the decisive defect is instead the unvalidated Unicode representation bridge, which materially excludes normal Python `str` values beyond the backend’s Latin-1-complete range. I’m writing the seven-stage report and trust ledger now.
